    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a critical slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker**, who represent our highest-ceiling plays at 81.88 and 81.23, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki, where a slow delivery increases his stolen base upside, combined with a 14% platoon edge and tailwind conditions. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is in a prime spot against Trey Gibson; the combination of a high-xERA opponent (5.63) and favorable wind provides the perfect environment for him to deliver elite production. **Andy Pages** (74.43) rounds out our strongest tier, as he also exploits the soft matchup against Gibson, providing high-leverage scoring potential alongside **Josh Jung** (63.35), who remains a locked-in start due to his impressive efficiency against Randy V\u00e1squez.\n\nWhile our starters are well-positioned, the decision to bench **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.55) was the most difficult of the day. Despite his high base talent, the optimizer favored the structural benefits and specific matchup advantages of players like **Coby Mayo** (54.73) and **Jackson Merrill** (52.46), as **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faced a tougher assignment against Beede. Risks remain across the board, particularly with our reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" status for players like **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin**. **Wade Meckler** (40.44) and **Dominic Smith** (40.91) are hovering near our minimum efficiency floor; while they provide utility, they are the first candidates to be pinch-hit for if early game conditions shift. We are carefully monitoring the weather and potential late-scratches, as our reliance on stolen base upside\u2014even against elite arms like Jacob deGrom\u2014requires us to remain agile if lineups deviate from our projected positions.",
